    "narrative": "For LawDog\u2019s May 29th slate, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (74.43) stands as our premier offensive anchor, thriving against Samaniego\u2019s 4.19 xERA and leveraging an ideal #2 spot in the order. He is joined in the \"Strong\" tier by **Matt Chapman** (69.89) and **Jonathan Aranda** (67.58), both of whom benefit significantly from favorable park factors and the 4.24/4.58 xERA matchups provided by Lorenzen and Ure\u00f1a. **Luis Arraez** (66.78) and **Jung Hoo Lee** (65.36) round out our most reliable options, with both players seeing a substantial boost from park-adjusted projections and positive platoon alignment against Lorenzen. While **Taylor Ward** (59.46) faces a tough 2.80 xERA arm in Macko, he remains a high-floor start because of his leadoff positioning and a positive platoon edge that keeps his efficiency just shy of the elite threshold.\n\nThe most difficult exclusion today was **Bryson Stott** (42.81), who narrowly missed the starting nine. Despite his potential for stolen bases\u2014a critical scarcity metric for LawDog\u2014the combination of a restrictive matchup against the southpaw Wrobleski and a lower raw efficiency projection relative to **Tyler Freeman** and **Geraldo Perdomo** forced him to the bench. We are also closely monitoring the availability of **Daulton Varsho** (57.38); while he slots in today, his moderate score reflects the volatility of a lefty-lefty matchup against Rogers. We remain without the services of **Cal Raleigh** and **Yainer Diaz** due to injury, leaving us reliant on **Will Smith** behind the plate, who faces the significant hurdle of a 2.86 xERA matchup against Wheeler today. We continue to manage our bench depth\u2014including **Lawrence Butler**, **Dylan Beavers**, **Gleyber Torres**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, and **Drew Gilbert**\u2014to ensure we maintain optimal efficiency across all 5x5 categories as we navigate the remainder of the month.",
